A||N||3||bHooper||Flywheel||||5
Z||000000||bHooper||11-01-1999||09:31 AM||||My 86.5 Gt sat for 2 years (outside under a car cover), without a transmission.  The flywheel as a mild coating of rust on the surface, what will need to be done for this?  I have read that it is bad to resurface a flywheel, as it will increase the gap that the pressure plate and clutch need to travel.<BR>Thanks,<BR>Brian||||reg||5
Z||000001||Tim||11-01-1999||10:08 AM||||Just knock the rust off with some sandpaper.  You can use a double action sander to make the job easier.  80 or 100 grit should do the job.  You want to remove the rust, not any metal.  You could also sandblast the flywheel then DA the surface.||||reg||1
Z||000002||bHooper||11-01-1999||10:30 AM||||DA?||||reg||1
Z||000003||Tim||11-01-1999||11:00 AM||||DA=double action=orbital <P>||||reg||1
